.so fork.tmac
.PP
.pt_pager_set_focus
.RS 7
.TP
.BI "dparms * " parms
An initialized
.B dparms
structure of a running
.B pager
instance.
.TP
.BI "int " requested_focus
Data source index of data line that should be in focus.
The value will be ignored if out-of-range, ie less than 0 or
not less than
.BR DPARMS :: row_count .
Use a value of
.I -1
to leave focus alone.
.TP
.BI "int " requested_top
Data source index of data line that should be the top row.
The value will be ignored if out-of-range, ie less than 0 or
not less than
.BR DPARMS :: row_count ,
or if the
.B requested_focus
cannot be accommodated by the request.
Use a value of
.I -1
to leave focus alone.
.IP
Typically, this argument will only be used to restore a previous
screen after using
.B requested_focus
to move.
.RE
.IP
This function allows a program to arbitrarily set a display position,
in a running instance, without going through user functions.  It was
designed for moving the position in response to a search.
.IP
The primary consideration is
.BR requested_focus .
The focus will be moved within an existing view if the requested
data line is alread in view.  Otherwise,
.BR DPARMS :: index_row_top
will be adjusted to an appropriate position that allows the focus
line to be visible.
